Subject: [PATCH] Add a byte to an alloc made during .mode -widths parsing. Bug
 report [bugs:9c07558565|2026-10-17T09:23:52Z].

[Hades: backport to 3.54.1 from branch-3.54. The release is the amalgamation, so the change is made where src/shell.c.in in shell.c.]

FossilOrigin-Name: 9373a2e3be798b2588bd81d7eb8292da7151534627ffa46130499daea4dd20cd
Upstream: https://sqlite.org/src/info/9373a2e3be798b2588bd81d7eb8292da7151534627ffa46130499daea4dd20cd
---
 shell.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/shell.c b/shell.c
index d3bbcc8..237a98f 100644
--- a/shell.c
+++ b/shell.c
@@ -34122,10 +34122,10 @@ static int dotCmdMode(ShellState *p){
         return 1;
       }
       zW = azArg[++i];
-      /* Every width value takes at least 2 bytes in the input string to
-      ** specify, so strlen(zW) bytes should be plenty of space to hold the
-      ** result. */
-      aWidth = malloc( strlen(zW) );
+      /* Every width value except a single-digit final value takes at
+      ** least 2 bytes in the input string to specify, so strlen(zW)+1
+      ** entries is plenty of space to hold the result. */
+      aWidth = malloc( strlen(zW)+1 );
       while( IsSpace(zW[0]) ) zW++;
       while( zW[0] ){
         int w = 0;
